@prefix as:   <https://www.w3.org/ns/activitystreams#> .
@prefix mem:  <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/mem#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# FALSE-POSITIVE WITHDRAWAL
# Claim under review: "the Pod has an 8-shape catalog but I count 11 shape files — that's a bug."
# Resolution: NOT a bug. The two numbers measure different things and both are correct.
# Recorded as mem:FalsePositive so the false-positive guard is itself auditable
# (per mem:FalsePositive rdfs:comment, and the worked example in the pod-curator skill's guard).

<urn:uuid:783AD2FD-7508-4FB3-BB5C-1A7738C7C2CC>
    a as:Announce, mem:RealignAction, prov:Activity ;
    as:actor <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    as:target </vault/wiki/working/curator-proposals/> ;
    as:object "claim: '8-shape catalog' contradicts 11 shape files" ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    prov:used
        </vault/meta/shapes/> ,                 # deployed Pod (operational truth — highest precedence)
        </vault/ontology/mem> ,                  # mem vocab scopeNote naming this exact false positive
        <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/mem#FalsePositive> ;
    mem:stalenessClass mem:FalsePositive ;
    mem:rationale """The flag is withdrawn — there is no bug. '8-shape catalog' and '11 shape files' are
correct at different granularities and D98 reconciles them explicitly.

GROUND TRUTH (precedence order: deployed Pod > decisions log > prose summary):

1. Decisions log (D98, decisions.md:662): 'The wiki-memory L3 shape catalog comprises
   8 SHACL NodeShapes (11 shape files total).' The number 8 counts NodeShapes; 11 counts files.
   D98 enumerates the 8 NodeShapes (Page, Thing, Concept, Person, Place, Event, Organization, HowTo)
   plus 3 additional files (WorkingNoteShape, resource.shacl.ttl D38 guard, template.shacl.ttl D100)
   = 11 files. The '8-shape catalog' phrasing in MEMORY.md is shorthand for the 8 NodeShapes; it was
   never a claim about file count.

2. mem vocabulary (deployed, /vault/ontology/mem): the mem:StalenessDetected scopeNote literally names
   this case as a CAUTION — 'before flagging a scalar/count claim, dereference the canonical decision —
   the reconciliation may already be written there (the 8-vs-11 false positive of 2026-05-23).' The
   substrate anticipated this exact flag.

3. Deployed Pod (/vault/meta/shapes/, operational truth): the live catalog now holds 18 .shacl.ttl
   files, not 11. The extras beyond D98's 11 are NOT drift — they are additive overlay shapes shipped
   after D98:
     - wiki-memory overlay also ships source.shacl.ttl + class-extension.shacl.ttl (wiki:Source
       re-introduced 2026-05-23 VIA the class-extension contract — a worked example, not a D77 relic);
     - addressbook overlay (D87/D88): contact-card, organization-card, membership, group;
     - owner-identity overlay (D89/D90): webid-profile, pod-owner-preferences.
   These belong to different overlays/profiles and are correctly outside the wiki-memory L3 NodeShape
   count. The '8-shape catalog' figure is scoped to wiki-memory L3 and remains accurate.

CONCLUSION: NodeShapes != files != deployed files-across-all-overlays. The claim conflated a
NodeShape count with a file count. No substrate change is warranted. If anything is stale it is the
NOTE that read '8 shapes = 11 files' as if they should match — but D98 already states both numbers
together, so even the prose is correct at source. Withdrawn.

A genuinely useful follow-up (NOT a bug, optional): the MEMORY.md shorthand '8-shape catalog' could
carry the parenthetical '(11 files; 18 deployed across overlays)' to pre-empt re-triggering this guard.
That is a prose-clarity SHOULD, proposed only, not applied.""" ;
    as:published "2026-05-23T22:16:53Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:comment "Withdrawn flag. No N3 Patch and no repo edit proposed — the substrate is correct as deployed." .
